! mcp_bootstrap_p39.strap -- SERVICE ROUTINES TO EXTRACT INFORMATION
! FROM SYSTEM CARDS, printed page 39.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.46, header "PAGE NUMBER 39".
! docs/boot_plan.md M3.
!
! >>> THREE OF PRINTED p.38's FOURTEEN PREDICTIONS LAND HERE, ON THE
! VERY NEXT PAGE. <<<
!
! p.38 used fourteen symbols it did not define and SYN'd each from
! its own binary output.  This page DEFINES three of them, at the
! addresses p.38 said:
!
!   Y JCBC   002213.00   p.38 line 30's "BXEZ,Y JCBC"   -- line 4
!   Y TCPGO  002214.40   p.38 line 31's "BXLZ,Y TCPGO"  -- line 7
!   Y LIMC   002246.00   p.38 line 33's "BXEZ,Y LIMC"   -- line 44
!
! AND Y TCPGO WAS THE SHARPEST OF THE THREE.  p.38 line 31 prints
! "002214.72 46", whose ".72" has BIT 18 SET -- the half-word
! selector -- so the address is 002214.40 and not 002214.00.  Line 7
! here is 002214.40.  A reading that ignored bit 18 would have been
! half a word wrong and would have failed here.
!
! IT CONFIRMS FOUR MORE FROM EARLIER PAGES, which is the same
! cross-check running the other way:
!
!   S ROOF   002162.00   printed p.37 line 37   -- line 20 reads it
!   Y USB8C  002200.00   printed p.38 line 21   -- line 30 reads it
!   Y NLST   001775.40   printed p.36 line 31   -- line 34 compares
!   Y NOPUN  001775.40   printed p.36 line 31   -- line 40 compares
!   Y UER    002311.00   p.38's prediction      -- lines 6, 17, 18
!   Y UCBF2  002337.00   p.38's prediction      -- lines 9, 33, 39,
!                                                  51, 53
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THIS PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Fifty-six rows, fifty-three of them code.  Three entry points, one
! per card kind that printed p.38's dispositions branch to:
!
!   Y JCBC  (line 4)   the JOB card.  Two rows and out.
!   Y TCPGO (line 7)   the T.O.P. card.  Compares the card's first
!                      forty-eight bits against four masks in turn --
!                      Y GOMK, Y COMMK, Y CNGMK, Y UPDAT -- and goes
!                      to a different place for each.  The GO case
!                      sets a count field, tests the system-mode bit
!                      S YSMCD, clears S CORG and sets up Y LOL1 and
!                      Y LOL2 before branching to Y BCRD.
!   Y LIMC  (line 44)  the LIM card.  "CONVERT BCD ZEROS TO TRUE
!                      ZEROS" -- a six-bit byte loop over the card
!                      buffer replacing (2)001010, which is the same
!                      BCD ZERO printed p.24 line 13 writes with
!                      "LFI(BU,4),(2)1010,46", with a true zero.  Then
!                      two LF/SF pairs convert the limits to binary.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! "SF" IS A CONNECTIVE WEARING ANOTHER NAME, and this page is where
! it was found
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 52 is "SF(BU,18,3),$12" and the assembler did not know it.
! The printed word is
!
!     002254.00   000034.00 80   022300.12 F0
!
! and the trailing F0 is CM, Connect to Memory (C prints 70, CT 77).
! The ".12" is bits 18-23 of the right half word, whose bits 19-22
! are the CONNECTIVE FUNCTION: 0101, five.  CM0011 renders ".06" and
! does not match; CM0101 renders ".12" and does.
!
! AND THE PAIR MAKES SENSE AS A PAIR.  "LF" was already known to be
! C0011 (strap/strap_asm.py CONNECTIVE_ALIASES, from printed p.5
! line 12).  A connective's four bits are a TRUTH TABLE over
! (accumulator bit, memory bit), so 0011 and 0101 are the two
! operand-SELECTING functions: LOAD FIELD takes the memory operand
! into the accumulator with C, STORE FIELD takes the accumulator
! operand into memory with CM.  Same datapath, the other projection,
! the other half of the table.  Line 51's LF and line 52's SF are
! adjacent rows doing exactly that.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! SUBSTITUTIONS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) BLANKS INSIDE SYMBOL NAMES ARE DROPPED, as on every page since
!     p.2.  Note that this listing's STATEMENT column already prints
!     them without blanks -- "LV,$13,SROOF" where the NAME column on
!     printed p.37 prints "S ROOF" -- so the substitution is visible
!     here as the two columns disagreeing, which is what makes it
!     safe.
!
! (2) "S CORG" IS NOT "S COM RG".  Line 19 is "CM0000(BU,1),SCORG"
!     with a left address of 002151.03 -- word 0o2151, BIT 3 -- and
!     printed p.37 line 11 puts S COM RG at 002151.00 with the
!     comment "THE SYSTEM WORD FLAG".  So S CORG is a one-bit flag
!     INSIDE the word S COM RG names, three bits in, and the two are
!     different symbols for overlapping storage.  Both are carried
!     here, and the addresses are read off the binary rather than
!     assumed from the similar spelling.
!
! (3) NOTHING ELSE.  Every glyph reads cleanly at 900 dpi.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE STAND-IN SYNs, AND WHERE EACH ADDRESS COMES FROM
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! A VFL instruction's LEFT half word is a clean twenty-four bit BIT
! address -- eighteen bits of word and six of bit, with no J field in
! it -- so the K/L/CM rows give their operand's address directly.  A
! HALF-WORD instruction's ".bb" is bits 18-23 and has to be decoded:
! bit 18 the half-word selector, 19-22 the J field, 23 the first bit
! of the operation code.
!
!   Y NORR   002313.40  lines 5, 11, 32, 43 -- FOUR rows, ".72",
!                       ".76", ".73" and ".50", every one bit 18 SET
!   Y GOMK   002354.00  line 10, VFL left address
!   Y COMMK  002362.00  line 12, VFL left address
!   Y CNGMK  002363.00  line 14, VFL left address
!   Y UPDAT  002365.00  line 16, VFL left address
!   S YSMCD  002151.10  line 18's left, a BIT address: word 0o2151
!                       bit 0o10, which is bit 8
!   S CORG   002151.03  line 19's left, bit 3 of the same word
!   Y LOL2   005464.40  line 21, ".73", bit 18 SET
!   Y LOL1   005465.00  line 23, ".33", bit 18 clear -- and line 24
!                       CONFIRMS it independently, since
!                       "Y LOL1+.25" prints 005465.31 and 0o31 is 25
!   Y BCRD   005464.00  line 25, ".10", bit 18 clear
!   Y UCX12  002322.00  line 44, ".30", bit 18 clear
!   S TERMI  005465.40  line 55, ".70", bit 18 SET
!   Y UCLLC  002262.00  line 56, ".32", bit 18 clear
!
! FOUR OF THEM ARE AT 0054xx, which is nowhere near this page: 005464
! through 005465, just below X IN END at 005466.  They are in the
! buffer area, on pages not yet opened.

        SLC, (8)2213.0

YNORR   SYN, (8)2313.40
YUER    SYN, (8)2311.0
YUCBF2  SYN, (8)2337.0
YGOMK   SYN, (8)2354.0
YCOMMK  SYN, (8)2362.0
YCNGMK  SYN, (8)2363.0
YUPDAT  SYN, (8)2365.0
SYSMCD  SYN, (8)2151.10
SCORG   SYN, (8)2151.03
SROOF   SYN, (8)2162.0
YLOL2   SYN, (8)5464.40
YLOL1   SYN, (8)5465.0
YBCRD   SYN, (8)5464.0
YUSB8C  SYN, (8)2200.0
YNLST   SYN, (8)1775.40
YNOPUN  SYN, (8)1775.40
YUCX12  SYN, (8)2322.0
STERMI  SYN, (8)5465.40
YUCLLC  SYN, (8)2262.0

        SLC, (8)2213.0

! ---- the JOB card -------------------------------------------------
YJCBC   KV, $13, 1.0($14)           ! line 4
        BXEZ, YNORR                 ! line 5
        B, YUER                     ! line 6

! ---- the T.O.P. card ----------------------------------------------
YTCPGO  Z, $12                      ! line 7  -GO - SET COUNT FIELD
                                     !           TO PROPER
        LCI, $12, (2)00100          ! line 8  -VALUE + GO TO NORMAL
                                     !           RETURN
        L(BU,48), YUCBF2+1.0        ! line 9
        K(BU,48), YGOMK             ! line 10
        BAE, YNORR                  ! line 11
        K(BU,48), YCOMMK            ! line 12
        BAE, YTOPCM                 ! line 13
        K(BU,48), YCNGMK            ! line 14
        BAE, YTOPCG                 ! line 15
        K(BU,48), YUPDAT            ! line 16
        BZAE, YUER                  ! line 17
        BZB, SYSMCD, YUER           ! line 18
        CM0000(BU,1), SCORG         ! line 19
        LV, $13, SROOF              ! line 20
        SV, $13, YLOL2              ! line 21
        Z, $13                      ! line 22
        SV, $13, YLOL1              ! line 23
        CM1111(BU,1), YLOL1+.25     ! line 24
        B, YBCRD                    ! line 25
        B, YUER                     ! line 26

YTOPCM  LCI, $12, (2)10011          ! line 27
        B, YTOPCG+.32               ! line 28

YTOPCG  LCI, $12, (2)01011          ! line 29
        LC, $15, YUSB8C             ! line 30
        KCI, $15, 2.0               ! line 31
        BZXH, YNORR                 ! line 32
        L(BU,48), YUCBF2+3.0        ! line 33
        K(BU,48), YNLST             ! line 34
        BZAE, $+1.32                ! line 35
        CM0000(BU,1), $12+.44       ! line 36
        KCI, $15, 3.0               ! line 37
        BZXH, YNORR                 ! line 38
        L(BU,48), YUCBF2+4.0        ! line 39
        K(BU,48), YNOPUN            ! line 40
        BZAE, YNORR                 ! line 41
        CM0000(BU,1), $12+.45       ! line 42
        B, YNORR                    ! line 43

! ---- the LIM card -------------------------------------------------
YLIMC   LX, $12, YUCX12             ! line 44 -LIM CARD- CONVERT BCD
                                     !           ZEROS
        LI(BU,6), (2)001010         ! line 45 -TO TRUE ZEROS
YLL2    CT0110(V+I)(BU,6), .6($12)  ! line 46 -IS THIS BYTE A BCD
                                     !           ZERO
        BZRZZ, $+1.32               ! line 47 -IF NOT TEST NEXT BYTE
        CM0000(BU,6), -.6($12)      ! line 48 -IF SO, REPLACE BY TRUE
                                     !           ZERO
        CBR, $12, YLL2              ! line 49
        BZXF, YLL2                  ! line 50
        LF(BU,36,6), YUCBF2+1.0     ! line 51 -LIMITS TO
        SF(BU,18,3), $12            ! line 52 -BINARY, PUT IN $12
        LF(BU,36,6), YUCBF2+2.0     ! line 53
        SF(BU,18,3), $12+.28        ! line 54
        KV, $12, STERMI             ! line 55
        BXL, YUCLLC                 ! line 56

        END, YJCBC

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! TWO LISTING MARKS, recorded and not explained -- the same bare "*"
! after the location that printed pp.3, 37 and 38 carry.  Here it is
! on line 14 ("002221.40 *"), line 32 ("002235.00 *") and line 47
! ("002250.40 *").  None changes a compiled bit.
